    name = "VPSS job node";
    desc = "Hi3516E V200 / V300 (shared SDK object hi3516ev200_vpss.ko, static analysis with scripts/tools/arm-trace, VPSS_HAL_Set* with the node pointer in argument 0, --keep-call-args, 230 words); cross-checked with scripts/tools/arm-emu (127 write offsets, 76 in common): the 51 extra words found only by arm-emu are 0x1800, 0x2000, 0x2004, 0x2008, 0x200c, 0x2010, 0x2014, 0x2018, 0x201c, 0x2020, 0x2040, 0x2044, 0x2048, 0x204c, 0x2050, 0x2054, 0x2058, 0x205c, 0x2080, 0x2084, 0x2088, 0x208c, 0x2090, 0x2094, 0x2098, 0x209c, 0x4000, 0x4004, 0x4008, 0x400c, 0x4010, 0x4014, 0x4018, 0x401c, 0x4020, 0x4040, 0x4044, 0x4048, 0x404c, 0x4050, 0x4054, 0x4058, 0x405c, 0x6040, 0x6044, 0x6048, 0x604c, 0x6050, 0x6054, 0x6058, 0x605c (PROVEN offsets from the emulator, not in the table below). Most of these words are a DDR job-node image written through argument 0 (ev200b: only 0x010, 0xF0, 0xFC, 0x200-0x2F0, 0x2F8, 0x300, 0x304, 0x308, 0x310, 0x314 are MMIO, those are in eVPSS_V4). Name/meaning of every word UNKNOWN unless stated. NOT A REGISTER FILE unless stated: register image / table written by the traced functions. PROVENANCE LABELS: PROVEN = read from the instruction stream (offset, stored byte lanes, cleared bit extents, ORed constants); INFERRED = role deduced from names or sibling chips; UNKNOWN = everything else. Source: symbolic trace of the module disassembly (arm-trace). Branches are linearized, extents are lower bounds. Not hardware verified.";

