regfile eVGS_NODE_V4_EV300 {
    name = "VGS node";
    desc = "Hi3516E V200 / V300 (hi3516ev200_vgs.ko, VGS_DRV_Set*Reg* with the node pointer in argument 0, 96 words; argument 1 gives none). The VGS job node is a DDR image, not MMIO (eVGS_V4 registers 0xF0..0x330 share no offset with it). Meaning of every word UNKNOWN unless stated. NOT A REGISTER FILE unless stated: register image / table written by the traced functions. PROVENANCE LABELS: PROVEN = read from the instruction stream (offset, stored byte lanes, cleared bit extents, ORed constants); INFERRED = role deduced from names or sibling chips; UNKNOWN = everything else. Source: symbolic trace of the module disassembly (arm-trace). Branches are linearized, extents are lower bounds. Not hardware verified.";

    reg {
        name = "Word 0x0";
        desc = "Word 0x0. PROVEN: stored byte lanes 0123, cleared bit extents none seen, ORed constants none, written by VGS_DRV_SetReg_ModuleCtrl (1 stores). Meaning UNKNOWN.";
